<title>BRAZIL: Barrier removed to Brazil CVRD sell-off.</title>
<headline>Barrier removed to Brazil CVRD sell-off.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian Senate Wednesday agreed to shelve a bill linking the privatization of mining conglomerate Vale do Rio Doce to congressional approval, officials said.</p>
<p>Officials said the Senate vote removed all existing legislative hurdles in the way of CVRD's sell-off.</p>
<p>The motion was put forward by Sen. Jose Eduardo Dutra, who had drawn up the bill.</p>
<p>The Senate vote also annulled a substitute version of Dutra's bill which had sought to dedicate revenue from Vale's privatization to regional infrastructure projects.</p>
<p>-- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358</p>
